"registration have already been initialized; use ``spacing`` and "
"``registration`` to override these values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/triangulate.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.triangulate.triangulate.regular_grid:83
msgid ""
"Name of the output netCDF grid file. If not specified, will return an :class:"
"`xarray.DataArray` object. For writing a specific grid file format or "
"applying basic data operations to the output grid, see :gmt-docs:`gmt."
"html#grd-inout-full` for the available modifiers. The interpolation is "
"performed in the original coordinates, so if your triangles are close to the "
"poles you are better off projecting all data to a local coordinate system "
"before using ``triangulate`` (this is true of all gridding routines) or "
"instead select :gmt-docs:`sphtriangulate <sphtriangulate.html>`."
msgstr ""

